          { name: "Cultural/Values Divisiveness", tag: "avoid", why: "The 2024 unopposed result indicates either consensus or low engagement, not ideological fervor. With median age 36.4 and a property-owning majority focused on tangible household economics, culture-war signaling wastes credibility and time. Candidates should avoid gratuitous partisan identity language and instead frame policy around shared material interests—taxes, schools, jobs, safety—that cut across demographic lines." }
