          { name: "Overlooking the 30.1% College-Educated Constituency", tag: "avoid", why: "While 30.1% college attainment is below South Carolina's state average, it represents a meaningful constituency of educated professionals and knowledge workers whose legislative priorities — education funding, public health infrastructure, environmental quality — can differ significantly from working-class homeowners. Treating SC-HD-19 as a simple working-class district without acknowledging that nearly one-third of adults hold college degrees risks missing a swing constituency that votes on different issues and is more likely to organize around specific policy failures. This group is also more likely to engage in local civic organizations and to influence local opinion — disproportionate political influence relative to sheer size." }
