          "Engage Hispanic/Latino and other minority communities with specific constituent attention and economic messaging: at 12.6% Hispanic and roughly 13% Black, Asian, and other communities combined, these groups represent the swing constituency in a 68-32 district—small business support for Hispanic entrepreneurs and career pathways for professional minorities are the issues most likely to durably shift voting patterns.",
          "Serve the 24.9% renter constituency explicitly on housing policy and affordability: while homeowners dominate at 75%, a quarter of residents rent, and in an environment of rising housing costs this constituency is evaluable and persuadable if a representative demonstrates concrete work on rental market conditions and affordable housing access.",
          "Strengthen the 68% by demonstrating legislative effectiveness on issues that matter to this district's professionals and families: educational funding and school choice, tax structure fairness, business-friendly regulatory environment, and infrastructure quality are the specific policy levers that keep a high-income, college-educated constituency from exploring alternatives."
