          { name: "Youth Disengagement and Economic Pessimism", tag: "careful", why: "The 32.4-year median age combined with 53.7% renter rate and 16.9% college attainment identifies a younger constituency that does not anticipate significant economic mobility through higher education and is evaluating options based on immediate job opportunity and cost-of-living reality. Young adults in this district are more likely to be apartment-bound, precarious-employment-dependent, and skeptical of government solutions — a demographic group that can swing toward populist or anti-incumbent messaging when they perceive establishment candidates are not addressing their constraints. The unopposed 2024 race means this constituency has not seen the incumbent actively compete for their support; a challenger who speaks directly to their economic situation can mobilize this disengaged cohort." },
          { name: "Treating the Incumbent's 2024 Unopposed Victory as Evidence of Durable Strength", tag: "avoid", why: "An unopposed result is not a vote of confidence; it is an absence of challenge. The 2024 Democratic win tells us that no Republican mounted a campaign, not that voters enthusiastically support the incumbent. With $40,145 income, 53.7% renter rate, 16.9% college attainment, and 32.4-year median age, this district is economically stressed and demographically younger — precisely the profile that swings to challengers who offer concrete solutions to material constraints. A 2026 Republican candidate must enter this race treating it as genuinely open, not as a Democratic stronghold." },
          { name: "Assuming the Black Majority and Hispanic Population are Locked-in Democratic Votes", tag: "avoid", why: "Black and Hispanic working-class voters will shift their support to any candidate — regardless of party — who credibly demonstrates commitment to jobs, wage growth, and economic opportunity in their communities. The unopposed 2024 race means the incumbent has not had to defend her economic record with this constituency; a Republican challenger can position as offering real alternatives if the incumbent is perceived as not delivering on material concerns. Treating these communities as automatic Democratic votes, rather than as working families evaluating their representative's economic performance, is a strategic failure that opens the door to real opposition." }
