          "Lead with property tax fairness and school funding adequacy as proactive legislative priorities: at 22.7% college attainment and $67,442 median income, the district's working-class homeowners are directly exposed to both property tax increases and school quality concerns, and a representative with specific solutions on these issues builds durable constituent loyalty that survives electoral competition.",
          "Build a documented record of local economic problem-solving — rural broadband access, small business support, workforce development partnerships with local employers — that demonstrates constituent service competence; unopposed incumbency creates an opening for a challenger to claim the incumbent has been invisible, and specific local accomplishments are the most effective counter.",
          "Avoid the strategic trap of treating unopposed status as evidence of safe incumbency: the 2024 absence of opposition is not a forecast of 2026 or 2028, and a representative who consolidates only the existing margin and neglects the opposition's potential constituencies will be vulnerable if demographic shifts or a credible challenger energize the renter population or the unaccounted-for 3.5% gap."
