          { name: "Treating 100% Unopposed Victory as Evidence of Electoral Safety", tag: "avoid", why: "An unopposed race produces a 100% result that reflects the absence of a challenger, not necessarily genuine constituent satisfaction or electoral durability. In a district with working-class economic pressures and a transactional rather than ideologically inherited voter base, unopposed victories often mask latent opposition that emerges when a credible alternative candidate appears. Assuming that 100% translates to a stable floor in a contested election is a strategic error that invites vulnerability." },
          { name: "Ideological Positioning Without Material Economic Solutions", tag: "avoid", why: "With only 21.1% college attainment and a 42.2-year median age in a $65,207-income constituency, voters in HD-39 evaluate representatives primarily on whether they are solving concrete household problems — not on ideological positioning or partisan consistency. A legislative agenda focused narrowly on conservative messaging without specific, visible action on healthcare affordability, housing costs, or job security creates an opening for a challenger who offers material solutions. The unopposed cycle provides an opportunity to build that record before opposition emerges." }
