          "Lead with cost-of-living governance: the 27.4% renter rate, $57,483 median income, and 41.3-year median age describe a constituency experiencing real housing and healthcare pressure; specific legislative answers on property tax fairness, wage standards, and healthcare affordability in a lower-income district are the foundation of durable Republican performance.",
          "Build active constituent relationships in Black communities around economic development and workforce access: the 26.68% Black population is not inherently Democratic—it is currently voting Republican at a rate that produces the 64-36 margin; a representative who demonstrates concrete investment in Black economic opportunity, job training, and community partnership maintains Black voter performance and keeps the seat safe.",
          "Do not assume the 28-point margin is structural: in a district where 27.4% rent and median income is $57,483, an opposition candidate who campaigns aggressively on wage policy, healthcare, and economic mobility while consolidating Black voters to 75%+ turnout has a credible path to competitive performance; the current margin is held by incumbent performance, not demographic destiny."
