          "Lead with education system quality and school choice: at 43.6% college attainment and median household income in the top quartile statewide, this is a constituency that evaluates school quality as a primary governance metric and is receptive to both traditional public-school investment and education-choice messaging—whichever the incumbent can credibly own.",
