          { name: "Assuming Partisan Loyalty Without Demonstrating Responsive Governance", tag: "avoid", why: "In a working-class district where the median household income is $49,212 and 24.8% are renters, constituents evaluate representatives primarily on whether state government is improving their material conditions — not on abstract partisan alignment. An incumbent who campaigns on party identity without demonstrating concrete legislative results on job access, housing affordability, healthcare, and public safety creates an opening for a challenger who offers specific policy achievements, visible community engagement, and demonstrable responsiveness to the concerns that shape constituent daily life. Unopposed victory should prompt urgent reflection on whether the incumbent has actually earned the district's trust, not confidence that the trust is automatic." }
