          "Lead with housing and economic security specifics: at 40.2% renter rate and $47,113 median income, the constituency is experiencing real housing instability and cost-of-living pressure. Tenant protection, affordable housing development, and wage policy are not peripheral—they are the primary governance concerns for a plurality of voters in this district.",
          "Address the 18.1% college attainment rate as a workforce pipeline problem: identify specifically whether low college attainment reflects access barriers (cost, childcare, transportation), lack of awareness of pathways, or weak alignment between K-12 education and regional workforce demand. Legislate to remove the constraint that is most actionable.",
