          { name: "Assuming the Unopposed Margin Proves Long-Term Safety", tag: "avoid", why: "Unopposed victories can signal either strong constituent relationships or weak opposition organization—and only time reveals which. In a district with 26% minority population, significant economic vulnerability, and low college attainment, the assumption that current Republican dominance is durable or that future Democratic opposition is unlikely is analytically unsupported. An incumbent who campaigns as though the 2024 unopposed result proves long-term safety rather than using it as an opportunity to deepen constituent relationships is unprepared for the next competitive cycle if Democrats invest." }
