          "Lead with working-class economic security: at $47,100 median income and 42.9 median age, this is an older, property-owning but income-constrained constituency for whom fixed costs (healthcare, property tax, utilities) are rising faster than wages—make concrete solutions on these issues the center of the campaign message.",
          "Address the 31% renter constituency with specific housing and wage-growth messaging: renters in a district with 42.9 median age are likely younger, more economically anxious, and more responsive to candidates offering tangible solutions on housing affordability and labor market access—this is a persuadable swing group if engaged directly.",
          "Avoid any messaging that positions racial communities against each other or treats the near-tied demographic split (48.76% white, 45.96% Black) as a fixed partisan alignment: the 56-44 result suggests a significant number of Black and/or white working-class voters are open to persuasion based on economic performance and specific policy solutions rather than inherited party loyalty."
