          { name: "Partisan Messaging Over Constituent Problem-Solving", tag: "avoid", why: "Affluent, educated constituencies in suburban and exurban districts evaluate candidates primarily on problem-solving competence and constituent service rather than partisan positioning. An incumbent or challenger who leads with partisan rhetoric rather than specific answers to education funding, healthcare access, tax policy, or municipal service delivery will find this constituency unmoved. This district requires governance messaging, not political messaging; candidates who cannot articulate specific solutions to concrete constituent problems will not persuade voters here." }
