          "Engage the renter community (33.5%) and workforce challenges (24.7% college attainment) as core governance priorities: these constituencies have real constraints on economic mobility and are responsive to representatives who deliver concrete improvements in job training, affordable housing access, and education pathways rather than default partisan messaging.",
          "Build active relationships with employers and workforce development institutions in the district: at 38.6 median age with migration-risk younger adults, the representative who connects constituents to actual employment opportunities and advancement pathways is delivering material constituent service that creates durable political loyalty.",
          "Avoid the assumption that 100-0 is a stable equilibrium: in a heavily Democratic district, the real electoral risk comes from primary challenge or community disengagement if constituents conclude the incumbent is not delivering on economic mobility and opportunity — not from general-election competition."
