          "Address the college-educated professional community's specific concerns: higher education funding and workforce development matter in a district with 35.9% college attainment, and candidates who can speak credibly about STEM education, university partnerships, and professional opportunity retention are better positioned than those who treat education as a generic partisan issue.",
          "Monitor whether the 23.4% renter rate represents younger professionals or economically vulnerable households; if significant economic mobility barriers exist beneath the affluent aggregate income, a future challenger could organize renters around housing affordability and break the current Republican margin."
