          "Build specific messaging on cost-of-living, healthcare access, and property tax fairness aimed at the 40.5-year-old median-age white homeowners at $58,530 income; this constituency is not inherently hostile to Democratic governance but will evaluate based on whether they perceive the incumbent as addressing their material economic concerns.",
          "Invest in local organization and constituent outreach infrastructure that extends beyond election cycles—unopposed victories can mask organizational weakness or declining engagement, and the next competitive election may arrive suddenly if a credible challenger emerges who makes economic anxiety the central campaign theme.",
          "Address the college-education gap of 20.4% through workforce development, vocational training, and community college partnership messaging; this is a working-class constituency, and Democratic governance that delivers tangible economic opportunity is more durable than messaging alone."
