          { name: "Dismissing College-Educated Swing Voters as Reliable Republican Base", tag: "avoid", why: "The 51.2% college attainment rate is substantially higher than South Carolina state averages, and college-educated voters — particularly in affluent suburbs — are increasingly swing-prone on specific governance issues rather than ideologically locked. At this income and education level, voters care about whether government is efficient, whether their schools are well-funded, whether property taxes are manageable, and whether community institutions are functioning. A campaign that relies on cultural or ideological framing rather than demonstrating concrete fiscal discipline and constituent service competence is vulnerable to a challenger who speaks directly to the material governance concerns of an educated, affluent constituency." }
