          "Monitor college-educated swing voters and address governance competence directly: the 33% opposition in a 76.6% white, affluent district likely includes educated voters who are genuinely evaluating fiscal management and community outcomes. A challenger who reframes around specific governance concerns can move these voters if the incumbent appears complacent rather than actively demonstrating performance."
