          "Maintain constituent attention to the 22.64% Black community without framing it as a swing audience: Black voters in SC-SD-9 are not persuadable to the Republican margin at 70%, but their turnout and morale affect whether a Democratic challenger can build a credible challenge; routine constituent service and visible responsiveness to Black-community priorities sustain baseline satisfaction without attempting symbolic overreach.",
          "Recognize that the 25.1% renter rate is too small to drive electoral strategy but large enough to matter for policy messaging: younger renters' concerns about housing costs and economic mobility are real, but they do not dominate the electorate; acknowledging these concerns without subordinating homeowner-tax priorities maintains a reasonable tone while keeping the homeowner base secure.",
          "Avoid the strategic error of treating a 70-30 margin as permission to ignore the district or assume no credible challenger will emerge: a 70% result is durable only if the incumbent continues performing visibly on the routine competence issues that drove it, not as a permanent partisan floor that survives neglect or a local-government failure that unites opposition constituencies."
