          { name: "Dismissing the College-Educated Plurality as Reliably Republican", tag: "avoid", why: "At 35.2% college attainment, this district has a substantial educated constituency that in national politics has demonstrated willingness to split from traditional partisan alignment when it perceives governance failure or ideological overreach. While SC-SD-12 currently delivers 64% Republican, this constituency will evaluate on specific policy performance — healthcare, education, economic opportunity — not abstract partisan loyalty. Any legislative record that appears dismissive of education, healthcare access, or professional economic concerns risks activation of the educated plurality toward opposition." }
