          "Recognize the 43% Democratic opposition as affluent swing voters, not a marginal minority: college-educated suburbanites with household incomes above $84k will support Democrats if they perceive the Republican candidate as economically incompetent or damaging to their interests. The margin is vulnerable to credible Democratic opposition that emphasizes competence and protection of middle-class economic interests.",
          "Engage the 22.76% Black community with specific constituent attention on education quality, economic opportunity, and healthcare access; in a prosperous suburban district, Black voters are not monolithic and will respond to candidates who address their material concerns rather than default to identity-based messaging.",
