          { name: "Treating College Attainment (26.6%) as a Reliable Partisan Anchor", tag: "avoid", why: "At 26.6% college attainment — among the lowest in the data — this is not a college-educated professional constituency where educational credential alignment with institutional politics is a durable voter commitment. It is a working-class constituency where economic mobility, wage trajectory, and housing stability are the primary determinants of political satisfaction. A legislator who frames their agenda around abstract professional-class concerns rather than concrete bread-and-butter issues for a working-class constituency will find that demographic advantage is not sufficient to maintain constituent satisfaction or turnout." }
